<title>USA: Wickes Lumber calls 1996 &quot;transition year&quot;.</title>
<headline>Wickes Lumber calls 1996 &quot;transition year&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>VERNON HILLS, Ill. 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wickes Lumber Co, which reported a subsiantial loss in 1995 after a major restructuring, said Thursday 1996 was a &quot;transition year&quot; that saw the company return to profitability.</p>
<p>For the fourth quarter ended December 28, Wickes reported net income of $2.0 million, or $0.24 a share, compared with a loss of $15.4 million, or $2.50 a share, one year ago.</p>
<p>The company took a charge of $17.8 million in the period in 1995 to cover a restructuring of its operations. Wickes reported a loss from operations a year ago of $16.0 million.</p>
<p>Wickes is a building materials supply company.</p>
<p>The company's shares were up 1/4 at 5-5/8 before trading was halted Thursday afternoon.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
